    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5941?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "F99451 Assistant Professor of Leadership",
      "description": "F99451 Assistant Professor of Leadership | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) F99451 Assistant Professor of Leadership Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5941 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/28/2026 Back to Search F99451 Assistant Professor of Leadership Position Summary The Department of Educational Leadership at Northeastern State University invites applications for a full-time faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. This position is Oklahoma-based in Tahlequah, OK. The successful candidate will support graduate education through high-quality teaching, an active program of research and scholarship, meaningful university and professional service, and sustained mentorship of graduate students in the Master of Science in Leadership and Doctor of Education (Ed.D.) in Community-Based Leadership programs. The Ed.D. in Community-Based Leadership is an innovative, cohort-based doctoral program designed to prepare scholar-practitioners who create sustainable change through collaboration among educational institutions, tribal nations, nonprofit organizations, government agencies, and community partners. Through applied research and a Dissertation in Practice, doctoral students address authentic leadership challenges while developing evidence-based solutions that strengthen organizations and communities. This position offers an exceptional opportunity for an accomplished scholar-practitioner to help shape and grow a distinctive doctoral program. The successful candidate will play a significant role in curriculum development, doctoral student success, research initiatives, community partnerships, and the continued advancement of graduate education. Faculty members are expected to contribute to a collaborative academic culture that values innovation, applied scholarship, mentorship, and community engagement. Why Join the Department of Educational Leadership? The Department of Educational Leadership is committed to preparing ethical, innovative, and community-engaged leaders through graduate education grounded in research, collaboration, and professional practice. Faculty enjoy a collegial environment characterized by shared governance, interdisciplinary collaboration, and a strong commitment to student success. Faculty have opportunities to: Help shape a growing doctoral program with a distinctive mission. Mentor highly motivated master's and doctoral students in a cohort-based learning environment. Collaborate with faculty across disciplines on research, teaching, and community-engaged scholarship. Build partnerships with PK–12 schools, higher education institutions, tribal nations, nonprofit organizations, businesses, and governmental agencies. Develop externally funded research initiatives and interdisciplinary projects. Assume leadership roles in doctoral education, curriculum development, assessment, accreditation, and program innovation. Contribute to a department that values academic excellence, collaborative leadership, and meaningful community impact. Desired Characteristics The ideal candidate is a collaborative scholar-practitioner who is passionate about mentoring doctoral students, advancing applied and community-engaged research, and preparing ethical leaders capable of transforming organizations and communities. Successful candidates will demonstrate a commitment to innovation, interdisciplinary collaboration, inclusive excellence, and integrating scholarship with professional practice. They will embrace opportunities to build a nationally recognized doctoral program that prepares leaders to address complex educational and societal challenges through research-informed action. Primary Responsibilities - Graduate Teaching This position is intended for candidates with a broad foundation in organizational leadership and the ability to apply leadership theory, research, and practice across diverse organizational and community contexts. The department seeks a versatile scholar-practitioner whose expertise extends beyond a single sector or leadership specialization and who can engage with leadership challenges across educational institutions, nonprofit organizations, tribal nations, governmental agencies, businesses, and community-based organizations. Candidates should demonstrate the capacity to teach across multiple areas of leadership, mentor graduate students with varied professional backgrounds, and connect organizational leadership principles to complex, real-world challenges. Faculty responsibilities include a balanced combination of graduate teaching, scholarly research, doctoral mentoring, and professional service consistent with the mission of a comprehensive regional university. Responsibilities include: Teach graduate courses in the M.S. in Leadership and Ed.D. in Community-Based Leadership programs. Teach doctoral-level research courses in qualitative, quantitative, mixed methods, improvement science, practitioner inquiry, and Dissertation in Practice. Teach courses in leadership theory, organizational leadership, educational leadership, strategic leadership, ethics, policy, organizational change, and community-based leadership. Develop engaging online and blended graduate courses using Blackboard Ultra. Employ learner-centered instructional strategies that foster engagement, collaboration, and scholarly inquiry. Participate in curriculum development and continuous program improvement. Provide timely, substantive feedback that supports graduate student success. Doctoral Mentorship Chair doctoral dissertation committees from prospectus through final defense. Serve on dissertation and comprehensive examination committees. Mentor doctoral students in research design, scholarly writing, data analysis, and ethical research practices. Guide students through qualitative, quantitative, and mixed methods research. Foster collaborative learning communities within doctoral cohorts. Support students in presenting and publishing scholarly work. Scholarship The department values an active scholarship agenda that advances leadership practice and contributes to meaningful educational and community change. Faculty are expected to: Maintain an active research agenda. Publish in peer-reviewed journals and scholarly books. Present research at state, national, and international conferences. Pursue external funding and collaborative grant opportunities. Engage in interdisciplinary and community-engaged scholarship. Produce research that informs leadership practice, organizational improvement, and community development. Service and Leadership Faculty members are expected to contribute to the continuous improvement of graduate education through institutional leadership and professional service. Responsibilities include: Participate in departmental, college, and university committees. Assist with doctoral admissions, interviews, recruitment, and student retention. Contribute to accreditation, assessment, and strategic planning initiatives. Develop partnerships with schools, community organizations, tribal nations, nonprofit organizations, and governmental agencies. Provide leadership within professional organizations. Serve in departmental leadership roles such as curriculum development, doctoral program coordination, dissertation coordination, assessment, or graduate faculty leadership. Required Qualifications Earned doctorate (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) in Educational Leadership, Leadership Studies, Higher Education, Organizational Leadership, Educational Research, or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution. Evidence of successful graduate-level teaching. Demonstrated expertise in qualitative and quantitative research methodologies. Experience teaching graduate research methods and doctoral research courses. Experience chairing or serving on doctoral dissertation committees. Demonstrated success mentoring graduate and doctoral students. Experience teaching fully online and blended graduate courses. Demonstrated proficiency with Blackboard Ultra or comparable learning management systems. Record of scholarly productivity appropriate for appointment at the Assistant Professor rank. Excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with one or more of the following: Experience teaching in an Ed.D. or Ph.D. program. Expertise in community-based research, participatory action research, improvement science, implementation science, or practitioner inquiry. Experience with Dissertation in Practice models. Expertise in mixed methods research. Experience using statistical and qualitative analysis software (SPSS, R, NVivo, MAXQDA, or ATLAS.ti). Experience with cohort-based doctoral education. Record of successful grant writing and externally funded research. Experience with accreditation, program assessment, and continuous improvement. Experience integrating artificial intelligence, learning analytics, or emerging educational technologies into graduate teaching and research. Demonstrated experience developing partnerships with educational institutions, tribal nations, nonprofit organizations, governmental agencies, or community organizations. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to: Inspire and mentor graduate students as emerging scholar-practitioners. Design rigorous, engaging graduate learning experiences in online and blended environments. Guide doctoral students through every stage of the dissertation process. Teach advanced research methodology with clarity and rigor. Foster collaborative, interdisciplinary research. Build meaningful community partnerships that support applied scholarship. Balance teaching excellence with sustained scholarly productivity. Work collaboratively within a collegial, student-centered department. Advance the department's mission through innovation, service, and academic leadership. Areas of Teaching Expertise Preferred teaching expertise includes one or more of the following: Leadership Theory Organizational Leadership Community-Based Leadership Organizational Change Higher Education Leadership Qualitative Research Methods Quantitative Research Methods Mixed Methods Research Practitioner Inquiry Dissertation in Practice Research Design Ethics and Educational Policy Application Materials Applicants should submit: Letter of interest addressing qualifications and alignment with the position. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching philosophy. Statement of research agenda. Unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire). Contact information for three professional references. Salary is $61,070 with excellent benefits The projected hire date is January 4, 2027 Applications are accepted until November 1, 2026 NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m. on the date above. Department Information for Applicants Faculty teaching may include distance-based courses, including blended and fully online classes. Transcripts may be scanned, saved, and uploaded. An official/certified transcript is required upon employment. Please include on the application complete contact information for three references. IMPORTANT APPLICANT INFORMATION FROM HUMAN RESOURCES Northeastern State University is an Oklahoma State agency. In accordance with such, any applicant hired for this position must provide a Social Security card to Human Resources during the hiring process. Northeastern State University complies with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and is committed to equal employment opportunity. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5938?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "FP9879 Part Time Faculty",
      "description": "FP9879 Part Time Faculty | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) FP9879 Part Time Faculty Broken Arrow, OK, United States | req5938 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/21/2026 Back to Search Adjunct Instructor for Health & Kinesiology (Broken Arrow) Department: Health and\nKinesiology. Courses to\nbe Taught: H ED 1113 – Principles of Health and Fitness/Wellness. H ED 2213 –\nFirst Aid/Responding to Emergencies. Position Overview: The Department of Health and Kinesiology\nis seeking an Adjunct Instructor to teach undergraduate-level courses in the\nareas of Health and Wellness and First Aid/Responding to Emergencies. The successful candidate will be expected to facilitate\nstudent learning across a variety of instructional formats including online,\nin-person, and hands-on environments. Qualifications: Demonstrated subject expertise in the areas listed above\nDocumented experience in online teaching environments. Commitment to high-quality instruction and student\nengagement Master’s degree or higher in a relevant field (Doctorate preferred). Job Duties: Deliver instruction in online, hybrid, or in-person formats. Engage students in interactive and applied learning. Evaluate student performance and provide timely feedback. Collaborate with department faculty to maintain\ninstructional quality and consistency. Uphold academic integrity and inclusive classroom practices. Anticipated Start Date: 1/11/2027 Compensation:\n$800 per credit hour. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5916?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "F99459 Assistant Professor in Psychology & Counseling",
      "description": "F99459 Assistant Professor in Psychology & Counseling | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) F99459 Assistant Professor in Psychology & Counseling Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5916 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/28/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor of Counseling – Tahlequah Campus Job Description: The Department of Psychology and Counseling at Northeastern State University invites applications for a full-time faculty position in the M.S. in Counseling program. The M.S. in Counseling program is a CACREP accredited program with emphasis areas in Clinical Mental Health Counseling, Addiction Counseling, and School Counseling. The successful candidate will have the ability to teach in a variety of counseling courses, but particularly those pertaining to addictions counseling. A PhD in Counselor Education and Supervision is required. Dual licensure as an LADC and an LPC is preferred. NSU offers courses on all three campuses including Tahlequah, Broken Arrow, and Muskogee. The position is based on the Tahlequah campus. Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to teach addictions counseling courses and core counseling courses (both didactic and clinical, including supervision of practica/internship). All course delivery integrates technology. NSU seeks candidates with experience or who are willing to teach in blended and online formats when needed. Additional opportunities to teach summer classes for additional pay are available. Candidates are expected to maintain active membership and involvement with an appropriate professional organization (i.e. ACA, ACES, etc.). In addition to teaching, the position will involve student advisement, university service, and professional/scholarly contributions typically expected of a faculty member. The institution may revise the terms of this role based on changes in state laws or policies. Annual salary $57,610.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date:  January 2027 Applications will be accepted until: 10/11/2026 (Applications will be reviewed as they are received NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST, on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. Notice to applicants It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5915?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "F99741 Assistant Professor of Health and Human Performance/Athletic Training, Tahlequah",
      "description": "F99741 Assistant Professor of Health and Human Performance/Athletic Training, Tahlequah | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) F99741 Assistant Professor of Health and Human Performance/Athletic Training, Tahlequah Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5915 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/28/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor of Health and Human Performance/Athletic Training, Tahlequah Description of Position The Department of Health and Kinesiology at Northeastern State University is seeking an Assistant Professor of Health and Human Performance/Athletic training. Responsibilities 1. Twelve hours\nteaching load of undergraduate and graduate courses within the Department of\nHealth and Kinesiology. 2. Participate\nin college and department recruitment and retention efforts. 3. Participate\nin curriculum development and accreditation processes (CAATE). 4. Advise\nstudents within the department and 5. Maintain\nscheduled office hours. 6. Engage in\nscholarly activities internally or externally. 7. Collaborate\neffectively with department and college members. 8. Provide\nservice to the department, the College, and the University. 9. Collaborate with\nthe MAT Program Director on all recruitment and retention\nefforts specific to the MAT program. 10. Support the\nMAT Program Director and Director of Clinical Education in curricular\nplanning, compliance with CAATE standards and Higher Learning Commission\nrequirements. Qualifications 1. A doctoral degree in Kinesiology/Athletic Training or a related field is required.  Applicants who are in the process of completing their terminal degree and/or who are ABD will be considered. 2. BOC certification in good standing and eligible for Oklahoma State Licensure. 3. Two years of clinical athletic training practice/experience are preferred. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities 1. Evidence of\neffective teaching and scholarly work in exercise science/athletic training. 2. Capacity to\nteach across program levels (bachelor’s and master’s) 3. Ability to\nteach via instructional delivery methods including face-to-face, service-learning,\nand online. 4. Previous\ncollege/university teaching experience in an Athletic Training program. 5. Experience\nwith CAATE accreditation and clinical education coordination. Special Instructions to Applicants During the application process, the applicant will be required to upload a cover letter, a current curriculum vita, a statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial transcripts and contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. An official/certified transcript is required upon employment. Please address all questions to the department chair (Dr. MooSong Kim) at kimm@nsuok.edu or 918-444-3217. Annual salary $56,130.00 with excellent benefits Projected hire date: 01/11/2027 Applications accepted until: 11/08/2026 NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m. on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. Notice to applicants It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5914?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "X96558 Assistant Director Communications, Tahlequah",
      "description": "X96558 Assistant Director Communications, Tahlequah | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) X96558 Assistant Director Communications, Tahlequah Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5914 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/27/2026 Back to Search Assistant Director Communications, Tahlequah JOB SUMMARY This position is responsible for preparing and maintaining statistical data and maintaining all communication platforms for undergraduate admissions and recruitment. Compile and analyze data to support recruitment initiatives; support the Director of Admissions & Recruitment. MAJOR DUTIES Assists in the development of the university’s recruitment targets, markets and goals. Serves as the undergraduate administrator for Radius. Manage recruitment communication to support recruitment and enrollment initiatives for prospective students. Contribute to the development and quality assurance of enrollment funnel reporting, integrate results into predictive modeling and performance reporting. Evaluates functionality of Radius, including operational and technical troubleshooting. Serves as the undergraduate administrator for Slate. Manage and coordinate outreach to support recruitment and enrollment initiatives for current and prospective students. Manage Call Center. Plan and coordinate social media presence for undergraduate admissions and recruitment. Assists with training and onboarding of new admissions and recruitment staff. Supervises daily operations within the Communications area. Assists with planning, organizing, and supervising annual recruitment events. Gathers and maintains current knowledge of university programs and services. Assists in enrollment management efforts as needed. Serves on assigned committees. Performs related duties as assigned. KNOWLEDGE REQUIRED BY THE POSITION Knowledge of higher education recruitment best practices. Knowledge of university admission processes, degree options, and housing procedures. Knowledge of university programs and services. Skill in the operation of computers and job related software programs. Skill in decision making and problem solving. Skill in interpersonal relations and in dealing with the public. Skill in oral and written communication. COMPLEXITY/SCOPE OF WORK The work consists of maintenance and development of all communication platforms for student recruitment and enrollment management reporting duties. The high volume of student contacts contributes to the complexity of the position. The purpose of this position is to recruit students for NSU through various communication strategies. Success in this position contributes to the successful recruitment of students. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree from an accredited university. Experience sufficient to thoroughly understand the work of subordinate positions to be able to answer questions and resolve problems, usually associated with two to three years experience or service in a university recruitment or admission office. Possession of or ability to readily obtain a valid driver’s license issued by the State of Oklahoma for the type of vehicle or equipment operated. Must be capable of maintaining regular attendance. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree and previous experience with Slate CRM preferred. Annual salary $43,896.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date: 11/9/2026 Applications will be accepted until filled NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST, on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. NOTICE TO APPLICANTS It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5881?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "F99426 Clinical Assistant Professor, Rural Health Care, Vinita",
      "description": "F99426 Clinical Assistant Professor, Rural Health Care, Vinita | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) F99426 Clinical Assistant Professor, Rural Health Care, Vinita Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5881 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/4/2026 Back to Search Clinical Assistant Professor, Rural Health Care, Vinita The Northeastern State University College of Optometry invites applications for a faculty position in the clinics of the Rural Eye Program. Responsibilities This position is a combined assignment with direct patient care, clinical education duties, and administrative activities as assigned to manage clinical operations. The clinical assignments will be in one of the Cherokee Nation tribal health facilities in the northeast Oklahoma area. Experience Preference will be given to applicants who have completed a residency program. Administrative experience in a private practice setting is desired. Education Requirements Applicant’s qualifications must include the O.D. degree and eligibility for licensure to practice the full scope of Optometry in Oklahoma. Annual salary $115,008.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date: 01/04/2027 Applications will be accepted until: 12/01/2026 NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST, on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. Notice to Applicants It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
