    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5962?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "D99937 Director of Workforce Pathways and Experiential Learning",
      "description": "D99937 Director of Workforce Pathways and Experiential Learning | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) D99937 Director of Workforce Pathways and Experiential Learning Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5962 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/22/2026 Back to Search Director of\nWorkforce Pathways and Experiential Learning JOB SUMMARY This position will provide overall leadership and management for the\nRegional Workforce Pathways Ecosystem and serve as the primary administrator\nresponsible for implementation of projects activities. MAJOR\nDUTIES ●This position will oversee the operation of the RiverHawks Regional Workforce Pathways Center ●Supervise project personnel. ●Coordinate workforce credential development and Workforce Pell readiness activities. ●Lead employer engagement initiatives. ●Chair the Regional Workforce Advisory Board. ●Facilitate collaboration among Northeastern State University (NSU), Tulsa Community College (TCC) and Eastern Oklahoma State College (EOSC). ●Coordinate annual workforce symposiums ●Oversee workforce data collection and reporting ●Support sustainability planning ●Ensure project activities align with institutional goals related to enrollment growth, retention, completion and workforce outcomes. ●Chair the NSU Workforce Development Committee. KNOWLEDGE\nREQUIRED BY THE POSITION ●Knowledge of recruiting, academic advising principles, and student development theory. ●Knowledge of data analysis and reporting. ●Skill in the delegation of responsibility and authority. ●Skill in the operation of computers and job-related software programs. ●Skill in oral and written communication. ●Knowledge of federal, state and local laws related to student privacy and records management. ●Knowledge of state regents of higher education and RUSO policies. ●Knowledge of budget development and management principles. ●Skill in decision making and problem solving. ●Skill in interpersonal relations and in dealing with the public and area businesses. SUPERVISORY\nCONTROLS The Director\nassigns work in terms of program goals and objectives. The supervisor reviews\nwork through conferences, reports, and observation of program activities. GUIDELINES Guidelines\ninclude national standards set by national academic advising associations,\nOSRHE and RUSO policies, Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA)\nguidelines, Department of Education (DOE) regulations, and university policies\nand procedures. These guidelines require judgment, selection and interpretation\nin application. COMPLEXITY/SCOPE OF WORK ●The work consists of varied management and supervisory duties, as well as coordination of activities and programs. The variety of tasks to be managed contributes to the complexity of the position. ●The purpose of this position is to oversee the university’s workforce and experiential learning opportunities. Success in this position contributes to the successful recruitment, engagement, and retention of students. CONTACTS ●Contacts are typically with co-workers, other university personnel, faculty, staff, students, representatives of area businesses, and members of the general public. ●Contacts are typically to give or exchange information, to resolve problems, to provide services, to justify, defend or negotiate matters, or to motivate persons. PHYSICAL DEMANDS/ WORK\nENVIRONMENT ●The work is typically performed while sitting at a desk or table or while intermittently sitting, standing, or stooping. The employee occasionally lifts light objects. ●The work is typically performed in an office. SUPERVISORY\nAND MANAGEMENT RESPONSIBILITY This position directly supervises Workforce Coordinators with carrying\nresponsibilities and works with departments all across campus. MINIMUM\nQUALIFICATIONS ●Knowledge and level of competency commonly associated with the completion of a master’s degree in a course of study related to the occupational field. ●At least 5 years of experience in progressive management positions, Academic Affairs, Enrollment Management, service or related areas. ●Possession of or ability to readily obtain a valid driver’s license issued by the State of Oklahoma. ●Must be capable of maintaining regular attendance. ●Autonomous with strong communication skills. PREFERRED\nQUALIFICATIONS ●Experience supervising full-time staff. ●Experience managing budgets. ●Experience managing collaborative arrangements and projects. ●Experience in teaching or training and development. Annual salary $79,986.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date: 11/16/2026 Applications will be accepted until: 11/4/2026 NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST, on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. NOTICE TO APPLICANTS It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5961?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "N99706 Groundsworker, Tahlequah",
      "description": "N99706 Groundsworker, Tahlequah | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) N99706 Groundsworker, Tahlequah Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5961 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/22/2026 Back to Search Grounds-Worker, Facilities, Tahlequah JOB\nSUMMARY This\nposition performs duties in support of the department’s grounds maintenance\noperations. The purpose of this position is to operate a variety of equipment in support of department operations. Success in this position results in safe and well-maintained buildings and grounds. MAJOR DUTIES Assists with grounds maintenance activities; mows grass, cut weeds, clears brush, and rakes leaves. Plants trees, flowers, and shrubs; trims trees and shrubs. Collects litter from campus grounds; empties trash cans. Moves office furniture; assists with setting up for special events. Captures and relocates nuisance animals. Applies herbicide and pesticide. Operates a variety of equipment including a backhoe and dump truck. Operates hand and power tools, including chain saws, weed eaters, and lawn mowers. Cleans up storm damage. Assists with snow removal operations. Loads and unloads trucks. Transports materials and equipment to work sites. Provides support to other maintenance personnel. Performs related duties as assigned. KNOWLEDGE REQUIRED BY THE POSITION Knowledge of equipment operation and maintenance principles. Knowledge of trash compactor maintenance and operation principles. Knowledge of department policies and procedures. Skill in the operation of job-related tools, vehicles and equipment. Skill in oral and written communication. PHYSICAL DEMANDS/ WORK ENVIRONMENT The work is typically performed while standing, walking, bending, crouching or stooping. The employee frequently lifts light and occasionally heavy objects, climbs ladders, and uses tools or equipment requiring a high degree of dexterity. The work is typically performed outdoors, occasionally in cold or inclement weather. The employee may be exposed to noise, dust, dirt, and grease, machinery with moving parts, contagious or infectious diseases, or irritating chemicals. Work requires the use of protective devices such as masks, goggles, gloves, etc. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Ability to read, write and perform basic mathematical calculations. Sufficient experience to understand the basic principles relevant to the major duties of the position, usually associated with the completion of an apprenticeship/internship or having had a similar position for one to two years. Possession of a valid driver’s license issued by the State of Oklahoma for the type of vehicle or equipment operated. Annual salary $25,536.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date: 12/7/2026 Applications will be accepted until: 11/15/2026 NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST, on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. NOTICE TO APPLICANTS It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5959?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "X96473 Postsecondary Pathways Coordinator – Broken Arrow Region",
      "description": "X96473 Postsecondary Pathways Coordinator – Broken Arrow Region | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) X96473 Postsecondary Pathways Coordinator – Broken Arrow Region Broken Arrow, OK, United States | req5959 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/22/2026 Back to Search Postsecondary Pathways Coordinator – Broken Arrow\nRegion JOB\nSUMMARY This\nposition will coordinate workforce pathway development and concurrent\nenrollment expansion efforts throughout the Tulsa metropolitan service area. MAJOR DUTIES Work directly with students, families, counselors and educational partners to promote workforce credential pathways. Support college-going initiatives. Increase concurrent enrollment participation. Facilitate student access to career exploration opportunities. Support pathway advising events. Employer engagement activities. Workforce credential awareness efforts designed to strengthen educational attainment and workforce readiness. KNOWLEDGE REQUIRED BY THE POSITION ●Knowledge of recruiting, academic advising principles, and student development theory. ●Knowledge of data analysis and reporting. ●Skill in the delegation of responsibility and authority. ●Skill in the operation of computers and job-related software programs. ●Skill in oral and written communication. ●Knowledge of federal, state and local laws related to student privacy and records management. ●Knowledge of state regents of higher education and RUSO policies. ●Knowledge of budget development and management principles. ●Skill in decision making and problem solving. ●Skill in interpersonal relations and in dealing with the public and area businesses. SUPERVISORY\nCONTROLS The supervisor\nassigns work in terms of general instructions.  The supervisor spot-checks\nthe work as it is being done and spot-checks the completed work for compliance\nwith established procedures, work accuracy and the nature and propriety of the\nfinal results of the work. GUIDELINES Guidelines include national standards set by national\nacademic advising associations, OSRHE and RUSO policies, Family Educational\nRights and Privacy Act (FERPA) guidelines, Department of Education (DOE)\nregulations, and university policies and procedures. These guidelines require\njudgment, selection and interpretation in application. COMPLEXITY/SCOPE OF WORK The work consists of varied management duties, as well as coordination of activities and programs. The variety of tasks to be managed contributes to the complexity of the position. The purpose of this position is to oversee the university’s workforce efforts and experiential learning opportunities. Success in this position contributes to the successful recruitment, engagement, and retention of students. CONTACTS Contacts are typically with co-workers, other university personnel, faculty, staff, students, representatives of area businesses, and members of the general public. Contacts are typically to give or exchange information, to resolve problems, to provide services, to justify, defend or negotiate matters, or to motivate persons. PHYSICAL DEMANDS/ WORK ENVIRONMENT The work is typically performed while sitting at a desk or table or while intermittently sitting, standing, or stooping. The employee occasionally lifts light objects. The work is typically performed in an office. SUPERVISORY AND MANAGEMENT\nRESPONSIBILITY This\nposition may have direct supervision over assigned student workers and would\nwork with local businesses and other departments across campus. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Knowledge and level of competency commonly associated with the completion of a bachelor’s degree in a course of study related to the occupational field. Some skill or work experience in an area related to the position description. Possession of or ability to readily obtain a valid driver’s license issued by the State of Oklahoma for the type of vehicle or equipment operated. Must be capable of maintaining regular attendance. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience collaborating or communicating with others. Experience managing agreements, recruiting, or engaging others. Annual salary $43,956.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date: 11/16/2026 Applications will be accepted until: 11/04/2026 NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST, on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. NOTICE TO APPLICANTS It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
