    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5953?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "F99988 Assistant Professor of Music",
      "description": "F99988 Assistant Professor of Music | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) F99988 Assistant Professor of Music Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5953 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/20/2026 Back to Search ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF MUSIC TITLE: Assistant Professor of Music (Piano) REPORTS TO: Chair, Department of Music STATUS: Exempt LOCATION: Tahlequah JOB SUMMARY The Department of Music at Northeastern State University is seeking applications for a full-time appointment for Assistant Professor of Music (Piano). We are seeking a dynamic teacher/performer whose educational background, professional performing accomplishments, and pedagogy will assist in recruiting and retaining students to NSU’s  Department of Music. The primary responsibility of this position is teaching applied piano lessons in both the classical and jazz idioms; additional teaching duties could include courses such as class piano, general education music courses, and courses in the Jazz and Commercial Music major based on the successful candidate’s background and expertise. The successful candidate will be expected to build a career of first regional and national distinction as a pianist and pedagogue. The ability to recruit and retain a studio of applied piano majors and minors is paramount to this position. Participation in university committees and departmental service through recital hearings, juries, auditions, recruitment, studio class, and other activities is expected. Teach applied piano to undergraduate music majors, minors, and nonmajors Perform with the jazz faculty Mentor and guide students in professional activities Recruit and retain applied piano students (music majors and minors) Engage in meaningful service to the Department of Music, as assigned Collaborate with faculty in the development of the program, curriculum content and pedagogy to ensure the quality of the student experience and student recruitment Required Degree Earned doctorate degree or masters degree with equivalent professional experience in classical or jazz piano performance. Doctoral candidates who are ABD at the time of application will be considered. Minimum Requirements Experience\nteaching applied piano Prior\nexperience teaching at the collegiate level Experience\nteaching class piano Performance\nand teaching expertise in both classical and jazz/commercial genres Ability\nto recruit, retain, and mentor a studio of piano majors, minors, and nonmajor Preferred Qualifications Preference may be given to applicants with a completed DMA or equivalent advanced degree. Significant career as a professional pianist in both the jazz and classical idioms Significant administrative and leadership skills Pedagogue in the jazz tradition, bebop and related harmonic concepts Required Application Materials To apply, submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, links to video recordings of 3 pieces that adequately reflect your strengths in both classical and jazz settings, links to a 30 minute unedited video of the candidate teaching an applied piano lesson or group piano class, 1 page statement of teaching philosophy, and the names/contact information for four professional references. Review of Applications begins on December 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to the committee chair, Dr. Jordan VanHemert, Associate Professor of Music at vanhemer@nsuok.edu. Annual salary $54,090.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date: 8/1/2027 Applications will be accepted until: 12/1/2026 NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST, on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. NOTICE TO APPLICANTS It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5952?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "N96569 Direct Admission University Representative",
      "description": "N96569 Direct Admission University Representative | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) N96569 Direct Admission University Representative Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5952 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/20/2026 Back to Search Direct Admission University Representative,Tahlequah JOB\nSUMMARY This position is responsible for recruitment of students\nto NSU through direct admission partnerships with high schools. MAJOR DUTIES Serve as the front line recruitment representative to direct admission partner high schools. Recruits students through oral presentations, college and career fairs, written and electronic communications, and individual contacts. Maintains relationships with prospective students from first contact through enrollment; serves as university liaison to prospective students, parents, and high school counselors. Establishes and maintains relationships with direct admission partner personnel supporting student success. Facilitate outreach, recruitment events, and campus tours for direct admission prospective students. Provide information regarding university, general education, and academic program requirements leading to successful matriculation. Conduct, at direct admission partner schools, workshops, orientation sessions, family information sessions, and other events targeting the strategic enrollment outcomes for the University. Schedule and organize all NSU transfer recruitment events at TCC and other Smart Choice institutions. Complete cross training with Student Transitions and University Advising and assist in advising prospective and admitted students as necessary. Develop strategic communication campaigns to increase direct admission yield rates. Main point of contact for direct admission outreach. Request student directory information from direct admission partner schools. Co-coordinate, with Tour Coordinator, direct admission partner schools’ group tours. Promote the direct admission partnership opportunity to non-partner high schools and ensure its understanding as a seamless integration at Northeastern State University. Performs related duties as assigned. KNOWLEDGE REQUIRED BY THE POSITION Excel in communication and customer service Ability to work with diverse populations of people, establish and maintain rapport Event planning, attention to detail, time management skills Ability to retain information and data, ongoing training, good communication skills Skilled in communication and presenting in front of a wide range of audiences Ability to communicate effectively with diverse student populations Short and long term goal planning, excel in written and oral communication SUPERVISORY\nCONTROLS The supervisor assigns work in terms of general\ninstructions requiring judgement to carry out assigned tasks. The supervisor\nspot-checks completed work for compliance with procedures, accuracy, and the\nnature and propriety of the final results.  It will be required to attend long term goal setting and strategic\nterritory management meetings that are held throughout the year to focus\nefforts. GUIDELINES Guidelines include department and university policies and\nprocedures, and OSRHE (Oklahoma State Regents of Higher Education) Policies.  These guidelines require interpretation and\nmust be accurate and consistent in the interpretations.  Every student’s situation is different and\nrequires attention to detail based on that information. COMPLEXITY/SCOPE OF WORK The work must be fluid and flexible.Within the University Policies and Procedures, you must be able to view all prospective students on an individual basis. Also, each communication with the academic colleges is unique and must be detailed regarding each academic program. This position is responsible for Recruitment of transfer students to NSU. CONTACTS Contacts are typically with internal and external college staff, Academic Deans and Associate/Assistant Deans, Academic Advisors, Faculty, Support Staff and Prospective Students. Contacts are typically to give or exchange information; to promote the university and our academic programs, and to provide educational opportunities for students to attain their academic goals. PHYSICAL DEMANDS/ WORK ENVIRONMENT The work is typically performed while sitting at a desk or while intermittently sitting, standing, or stooping. The employee occasionally lifts light and/or heavy objects. The work is typically performed in an office, library or computer room. SUPERVISORY AND MANAGEMENT\nRESPONSIBILITY None. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Knowledge and level of competency commonly associated with completion of a Bachelor’s degree A minimum of 1-3 years of experience in higher education, marketing, or enrollment management with specific training as it relates to NSU and our academic program offerings. A valid Oklahoma Driver’s License Must be capable of maintaining regular attendance. This position requires substantial travel and irregular hours, including nights and weekends. PREFERRED QUALIFICATION Master’s degree preferred Annual salary $36,084.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date: 11/9/2026 Applications will be accepted until: 11/2/2026 NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST, on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. NOTICE TO APPLICANTS It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5926?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "N99498 Administrative Secretary, Transfer Student Services, Tahlequah",
      "description": "N99498 Administrative Secretary, Transfer Student Services, Tahlequah | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) N99498 Administrative Secretary, Transfer Student Services, Tahlequah Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5926 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/19/2026 Back to Search Administrative Secretary,  Transfer Student Services, Tahlequah JOB\nSUMMARY This position provides secretarial support for assigned\nuniversity operations. MAJOR DUTIES Prepares a variety of correspondence. Makes travel arrangements for assigned personnel. Answers telephone and greets visitors; provides information and assistance; takes messages; refers to appropriate personnel. Maintains office supply inventory; reorders as needed. Sorts and distributes mail. Makes appointments and manages calendars. Processes purchase orders; processes purchase card statements. Maintains a variety of documents and forms. Directs the work of student employees as assigned. Enters information to computerized databases. Prepares a variety of schedules and calendars. Performs related duties. KNOWLEDGE REQUIRED BY THE POSITION Knowledge of university policies and procedures. Knowledge of modern office practices and procedures. Knowledge of computers and job-related software programs. Skill in the provision of customer services. Skill in oral and written communication. SUPERVISORY\nCONTROLS The supervisor assigns work in terms of general\ninstructions. The supervisor spot-checks completed work for compliance with\nprocedures, accuracy, and the nature and propriety of the final results. GUIDELINES Guidelines include department and university policies and\nprocedures. These guidelines are generally clear and specific, but may require\nsome interpretation in application. COMPLEXITY/SCOPE OF WORK The work consists of related secretarial duties. Frequent interruptions contribute to the complexity of the position. The purpose of this position is to provide secretarial support for assigned university operations.Success in this position contributes to the efficiency and effectiveness of those operations. CONTACTS Contacts are typically with co-workers, other college personnel, students, faculty, and members of the general public. Contacts are typically to provide services, to give or exchange information, or to resolve problems. PHYSICAL DEMANDS/ WORK ENVIRONMENT The work is typically performed while sitting at a desk or while intermittently sitting, standing, walking, bending, crouching or stooping. The employee frequently lifts light and occasionally heavy objects. The work is typically performed in an office. SUPERVISORY AND MANAGEMENT\nRESPONSIBILITY This\nposition may have functional supervision over student workers as assigned. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Ability to read, write and perform mathematical calculations at a level commonly associated with the completion of high school or equivalent. Sufficient experience to understand the basic principles relevant to the major duties of the position, usually associated with the completion of an apprenticeship/internship or having had a similar position for one to two years. Annual salary $25,536.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date: 11/30/2026 Applications will be accepted until: 11/01/2026 NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST, on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. NOTICE TO APPLICANTS It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5948?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "FP9868 Part-time Faculty - Music",
      "description": "FP9868 Part-time Faculty - Music | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) FP9868 Part-time Faculty - Music Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5948 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/12/2026 Back to Search Artist Instructor of\nMusic Tahlequah Notice to Applicants It is Northeastern State\nUniversity’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original\nsocial security card during the hiring process. Failure to provide an original\nsocial security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Description of Position The Department of Music at Northeastern State University is\nseeking a highly qualified artist for undergraduate level applied instruction. Chamber music coaching, core music courses, and general\neducation courses are also a possibility, depending on departmental needs and\ncandidate’s qualifications. Experience Previous teaching experience preferred. Education requirements Master's degree in appropriate\ndiscipline required to teach undergraduate courses; Doctorate required to teach\ngraduate level courses. Non-tenure track Salary $375 per credit hour for applied\nlessons. $800 per traditional course credit hour (typically $2400 per 3 hour\ncourse). Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5969?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "F99820 Assistant Professor of Social Work/ Broken Arrow",
      "description": "F99820 Assistant Professor of Social Work/ Broken Arrow | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) F99820 Assistant Professor of Social Work/ Broken Arrow Broken Arrow, OK, United States | req5969 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/29/2026 Back to Search F99820 Assistant Professor of Social Work, Broken Arrow Description of Position The\nCollege of Liberal Arts at Northeastern State University is seeking a highly\nqualified and motivated individual for a full-time Assistant Professor\nposition in the Social Work program. Teaching Responsibilities The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching undergraduate\nand graduate-level courses in social work, contributing to curriculum development,\nadvising students, engaging in scholarly activities, and participating in\nservice to the department, college, university, and community. This position\nreflects NSU’s ongoing commitment to academic excellence, student success, and\nthe preparation of future professionals who will serve diverse and dynamic\ncommunities. Required Education and Experience An MSW from a Council on Social Work Education (CSWE) accredited program A minimum of two years post-MSW social work practice experience A DSW/Ph.D. in social work or a related field is required. ABD candidates will be considered; however, all degree requirements must be completed by July 31, 2027. Teaching experience in micro, mezzo, and/or macro teaching experience Capacity to teach across program levels (bachelor's and master's) Ability to teach via various instructional delivery methods, including face-to-face, service-learning, and online Documents needed to apply Cover letter Current curriculum vita Statement of teaching philosophy Unofficial transcripts, Contact information for three professional references.  In addition, letters are requested from three references.  Review of applications will begin immediately. Official/certified transcripts are required for all degrees earned upon employment. Annual salary $58,290.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date: 1/4/2027 Applications will be accepted until: 11/22/2026 NOTE:  Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST,  on the date above.  An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. “Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis.” Notice to applicants It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5966?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "N99417 Administrative Secretary - Social Work",
      "description": "N99417 Administrative Secretary - Social Work | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) N99417 Administrative Secretary - Social Work Broken Arrow, OK, United States | req5966 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/29/2026 Back to Search Administrative Secretary, College of Liberal Arts, Tahlequah JOB SUMMARY This position provides administrative and clerical support to the School of Social Work and the Broken Arrow Liberal Arts Building. MAJOR DUTIES Answers telephone and greets visitors; provides information and assistance; takes messages; refers to appropriate personnel. Review and process personnel action forms including status changes, transfers, promotions and demotions, which are critical for payroll purposes. Compile data and prepare reports as directed. Types letters, memoranda, emails. Sets up and maintains personnel files and records. Processes departmental travel arrangements and reimbursement requests. Maintains office supplies; reorders as needed. Maintains office equipment. Sorts and distributes mail. Makes appointments and manages calendars. Process purchase orders; process purchase card statements. Maintains a variety of documents and forms. Performs related duties as assigned. KNOWLEDGE REQUIRED BY THE POSITION Knowledge of modern office practices. Knowledge of university human resources policies and procedures. Skill in meeting designated deadlines for work product. Skill in operation of computers and job related software programs. Skill in decision making and problem solving. Skill in interpersonal relations and in dealing with the public. Skill in oral and written communications. COMPLEXITY/SCOPE OF WORK The work consists of related secretarial duties. Frequent interruptions contribute to the complexity of the position. The purpose of this position is to provide administrative and clerical support for department operations.  Success in this position contributes to the efficiency and effectiveness of those operations. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Must be capable of maintaining regular attendance. Knowledge and level of competency commonly associated with the completion of specialized training in the field of work, in addition to basic skills typically associated with a high school education. Sufficient experience to understand the basic principles relevant to the major duties of the position, usually associated with the completion of an apprenticeship/internship or having had a similar position for one to two years. Annual salary $25,536.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date: 12/07/2026 Applications will be accepted until: 11/15/2026 NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST,  on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. Notice to applicants It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5965?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "X96555 Associate Director of Student Engagement",
      "description": "X96555 Associate Director of Student Engagement | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) X96555 Associate Director of Student Engagement Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5965 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/27/2026 Back to Search Associate Director of Student Engagement JOB\nSUMMARY Supervising\nthe student involvement team, this position provides leadership, program\nmanagement, vision and creativity to a dynamic team of professional and\nparaprofessional staff. This position oversees the NSU fraternity and sorority\ncommunity, provides ongoing leadership development opportunities for all NSU\nstudents, assists with Community Engagement efforts, and manages the student involvement\nteam. MAJOR DUTIES Provides leadership, vision, and supervision of the student involvement team within the Department of Student Engagement, with the support of the Director of Student Engagement and Transition. Areas of management includes: fraternity and sorority life, leadership development, community service and volunteerism, civic engagement, student organizations, and major events and campus programs. Creates a cohesive team unit through the implementation of professional development, coaching, and mentoring for the student involvement team members, including two full-time professional staff, a graduate assistant, and student workers. Advises officers and members of the fraternity and sorority governing councils and member chapters; advises individual members of the fraternity and sorority community and other members of the student body. Directly manages the overall fraternity and sorority program, including risk management, member education, planning annual retreats for governing council officers, and managing annual awards. Assists the governing council officers with formal and informal membership recruitment processes. Works with housing personnel and governing councils in regard to campus living. Advises Order of Omega. Maintains regular communication with fraternity and sorority chapter advisors, national/international headquarters, local alumni, community leaders, and University partners for both chapter management and leadership development. Coordinates Days of Service and community service programming.Manages the volunteer database, tracks and reports service hours. Provides civic engagement programming and education. Manages a broad based leadership development program for all NSU students.Provides ongoing outreach and training opportunities around topics of leadership development.Coordinates the leadership certificate. Updates and tracks strategic plans, learning outcomes, and assessments. Manages applicable budgets. Develops and maintains publications. Performs related duties as assigned. KNOWLEDGE REQUIRED BY THE POSITION Knowledge of student development and leadership development theory. Knowledge of fraternity and sorority operations, including Inter-fraternity, PanHellenic, National PanHellenic, and multicultural organizations. Knowledge of higher education law related to organizations and event risk management. Knowledge of budget development and management principles. Skill in the delegation of responsibility and authority. Skill in the operation of computers and job related software programs. Skill in decision making and problem solving. Skill in interpersonal relations and in dealing with the public. Skill in oral and written communication. SUPERVISORY\nCONTROLS The Director of Student Engagement and Transitions assigns\nwork in terms of program goals and objectives. The supervisor reviews work\nthrough conferences, reports, and observation of program activities. GUIDELINES Guidelines include the state and university purchasing\npolicies, Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act regulations, Title IX, ADA,\nprofessional advising standards, university policies and procedures, NPC Manual\nof Information, NIC guidelines, various multicultural and NPHC governing\ndocuments, and the NSU student code of conduct. These guidelines require\njudgment, selection and interpretation in application. COMPLEXITY/SCOPE OF WORK The work consists of varied management and supervisory duties, as well as coordination of activities and programs. The variety of tasks to be managed contributes to the complexity of the position. The purpose of this position is to oversee the university’s student involvement programs. Success in this position contributes to the successful engagement and retention of students. CONTACTS Contacts are typically with co-workers, other university personnel, faculty, staff, students, representatives of national and international Greek organizations, and members of the general public. Contacts are typically to give or exchange information, to resolve problems, to provide services, to justify, defend or negotiate matters, or to motivate persons. PHYSICAL DEMANDS/ WORK ENVIRONMENT The work is typically performed while sitting at a desk or table or while intermittently sitting, standing, or stooping. The employee occasionally lifts light objects. The work is typically performed in an office. SUPERVISORY AND MANAGEMENT\nRESPONSIBILITY This\nposition directly supervises Assistant Director of Student Engagement, Coordinator\nof Student Engagement, Graduate Assistant, and several student workers. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Knowledge and level of competency commonly associated with the completion of a master’s degree in a course of study related to the occupational field. At least 2 years’ experience in Student Activities, Greek Life, Leadership programming, or related area. Possession of or ability to readily obtain a valid driver’s license issued by the State of Oklahoma for the type of vehicle or equipment operated. Must be capable of maintaining regular attendance. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience supervising full-time staff. Experience managing budgets. Annual salary $53,544.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date: 1/4/2027 Applications will be accepted until: 11/16/2026 NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST, on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. NOTICE TO APPLICANTS It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5960?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "N99536 Certified Police Officer, Tahlequah",
      "description": "N99536 Certified Police Officer, Tahlequah | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) N99536 Certified Police Officer, Tahlequah Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5960 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/22/2026 Back to Search Certified Police Officer Public Safety ~ Tahlequah Campus JOB\nSUMMARY This\nposition is responsible for participating in law enforcement and public safety\nfunctions on an assigned campus of Northeastern State University. MAJOR DUTIES Enforces federal, state, and municipal laws. Prepares and submits reports. Investigates criminal activities; interviews suspects and witnesses. Attends weekly and monthly meetings with administration and departmental officials. Patrols campus on foot, on bicycle, or in an assigned vehicle. Enforces traffic regulations and issues citations. Enforces parking regulations and issues parking citations. Utilizes camera systems to monitor campus activities. Assists faculty, staff, students and visitors with locked vehicles and jump starts. Makes bank deposits. Performs related duties as assigned. KNOWLEDGE REQUIRED BY THE POSITION Knowledge of university policies and procedures. Knowledge of common law enforcement and criminal investigation procedures. Knowledge of federal, state and local criminal laws. Knowledge of public safety principles as related to college campuses. Knowledge of the operation of and legal requirements related to law enforcement equipment. Skill in decision making and proactive problem solving. Skill in the completion of a variety of reports. Skill in oral and written communication. SUPERVISORY\nCONTROLS The Sergeant assigns work in terms of general\ninstructions. The supervisor spot-checks completed work for compliance with\nprocedures, accuracy, and the nature and propriety of the final results. GUIDELINES Guidelines include local ordinances, state laws, federal\nlaws and standards, evidence laws, criminal investigation laws, and university\npolicies and procedures. These guidelines require judgment, selection and\ninterpretation in application. COMPLEXITY/SCOPE OF WORK The work consists of related law enforcement and public safety duties. The need to respond to unforeseen and potentially life threatening and dangerous situations contributes to the complexity of the position. The purpose of this position is to participate in law enforcement and public safety operations at an assigned campus. Success in this position contributes to the safety of university personnel, students, visitors, and property. CONTACTS Contacts are typically with co-workers, students, other university personnel, representatives of other law enforcement and public safety agencies, and members of the general public. Contacts are typically to give or exchange information, to resolve problems, or to provide services. PHYSICAL DEMANDS/ WORK ENVIRONMENT The work is typically performed outdoors or in a vehicle, intermittently sitting, standing, stooping, walking or running. The employee frequently lifts light and occasionally heavy objects, uses tools or equipment requiring a high degree of dexterity, distinguishes between shades of color, and utilizes the sense of smell. The work is typically performed in an office and outdoors, occasionally in cold or inclement weather or extreme heat. The work requires the use of specialized law enforcement and public safety tools and equipment, including the carrying of a firearm. SUPERVISORY AND MANAGEMENT\nRESPONSIBILITY None. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Ability to read, write and perform mathematical calculations at a level commonly associated with the completion of high school or equivalent. Sufficient experience to understand the basic principles relevant to the major duties of the position, usually associated with the completion of an apprenticeship/internship or having had a similar position for one to two years. Possession of a valid driver’s license issued by the State of Oklahoma for the type of vehicle or equipment operated. Ability to meet current requirements set forth by the Police Officer Standards and Training Certification for the State of Oklahoma. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS CLEET Certification Associates degree Annual\nsalary $38,844.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated\nhire date: 12/7/2026 Applications\naccepted until: 11/4/2026 Note: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 pm, CST, on the date above. Notice to Applicants At the end of the application process, create your candidate profile. It is Northeastern State University’s\npolicy that all newly hired employees must provide an original Social Security\ncard during the hiring process. Failure to provide an original Social Security\ncard will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. An application cannot be changed\nafter it has been submitted. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    }
